#. translators: Shown in the Language panel of the Site Editor for a template that WordPress still reads from a plugin's files (e.g. a WooCommerce block template), i.e. the user has not saved any change to it yet. WPML can only translate a template once a saved copy exists in the database; after that, updates of that plugin no longer change the template.
msgid "This template comes from a plugin. To translate it, first save a change to it in the Site Editor. After that, WordPress uses your saved copy, and updates of the plugin no longer change this template."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Shown in the Language panel of the Site Editor for a template that WordPress still reads from the theme's files, i.e. the user has not saved any change to it yet. WPML can only translate a template once a saved copy exists in the database.
msgid "This template comes from your theme. To translate it, first save a change to it in the Site Editor. After that, WordPress uses your saved copy, and updates of the theme no longer change this template."
msgstr ""
